  "about": "Sci-fi club: four on the floor, claps on 2 and 4 layered with a short snare and a few clap ghosts on the a, closed 16ths driving round open hats on every offbeat 8th, laser zaps as offbeat accents and pickups (a 3/16 laser roll in drop 2), a rolling octave bass that rests on every kick, answers it with the root on the e, leaps an octave with the accent on the offbeat 8th and ghosts the a, a wide starfield pad with slow CC74 movement (offbeat stabs in drop 2), and a sequenced chrome arp that follows the chords: cells that leap over the chord's ladder (root, third, fifth, seventh, two octaves) with a 3-3-2 accent, gaps on the a and the e, and its own filter. Builds roll up from claps on the beat to a 16th snare roll under a crescendo while the filters sweep up into the drop. Arranged as a DJ-friendly extended mix.",
